.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt DOAS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm doas
.Nd execute commands as another user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm doas
.Op Fl Lns
.Op Fl C Ar config
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl U Ar path
.Op Fl P Ar promise
.Ar command
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility executes the given command as another user.
The
.Ar command
argument is mandatory unless
.Fl C ,
.Fl L ,
or
.Fl s
is specified.
.Pp
The user will be required to authenticate by entering their password,
unless configured otherwise.
Authentication uses PAM; the service name is
.Dq doas .
.Pp
By default, a new environment is created.
The variables
.Ev HOME ,
.Ev LOGNAME ,
.Ev PATH ,
.Ev SHELL ,
and
.Ev USER
are set to values appropriate for the target user.
.Ev PATH
is set at compile time
.Pq see Fl -with-safepath
in
.Pa configure .
.Ev DOAS_USER
is set to the name of the user executing
.Nm .
The variables
.Ev DISPLAY
and
.Ev TERM
are inherited from the current environment.
This behavior may be modified by the config file.
The working directory is not changed.
.Pp
On Linux, two optional sandboxes are available.
A seccomp syscall filter is enabled by passing at least one
.Fl P ;
unlisted syscalls return
.Er EPERM .
A Landlock filesystem sandbox is enabled by passing at least one
.Fl U ;
when enabled, the sandbox is inherited across
.Xr execve 2 ,
so the command sees only the whitelisted paths.
Both are off by default.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width tenletters
.It Fl C Ar config
Parse and check the configuration file
.Ar config ,
then exit.
If
.Ar command
is supplied,
.Nm
will also perform command matching.
In the latter case
either
.Sq permit ,
.Sq permit nopass
or
.Sq deny
will be printed on standard output, depending on command
matching results.
No command is executed.
.It Fl L
Clear any persisted authentications from previous invocations,
then immediately exit.
No command is executed.
On Linux, this removes the timestamp file under
.Pa /run/doas .
.It Fl n
Non interactive mode, fail if the matching rule doesn't have the
.Ic nopass
option.
.It Fl P Ar promise
Enable the seccomp syscall filter for this invocation and add
.Ar promise
to the base promise set
.Pq Dq stdio rpath wpath getpw exec id .
May be specified multiple times.
The base set does not include
.Cm tty ;
programs that use
.Xr ioctl 2
on the controlling terminal
.Pq interactive editors, pagers, full-screen tools
need
.Fl P tty .
Without it,
.Xr ioctl 2
returns
.Er EPERM ,
which also blocks TIOCSTI tty character injection.
Networking syscalls
.Pq socket, connect, sendto, recvfrom, etc.
are currently part of the
.Cm stdio
promise, not a separate
.Cm inet
promise; any
.Fl P
invocation can open sockets.
Without any
.Fl P ,
the filter is not applied and the command has the full syscall
interface, matching stock
.Ox
behavior.
Enabling the filter also sets
.Dv no_new_privs
on the process, so setuid binaries executed under
.Fl P
do not regain privileges.
This is required by
.Xr seccomp 2
and cannot be disabled while
.Fl P
is in effect.
.It Fl s
Execute the shell from
.Ev SHELL
or
.Pa /etc/passwd .
.It Fl U Ar path
Enable the Landlock filesystem sandbox for this invocation and add
.Ar path
to the whitelist.
The executed command may access
.Ar path
and everything beneath it.
May be specified multiple times.
Without any
.Fl U ,
the sandbox is not applied and the command sees the whole filesystem,
matching stock
.Ox
behavior.
When
.Fl U
is used at least once, the sandbox is enabled and the command also
sees the core paths
.Pq libc, passwd, group, nsswitch, localtime, ssl, /dev/null, /dev/urandom, /proc, /sys
plus the binary itself.
The process is marked
.Dv no_new_privs
before the ruleset is installed, so setuid binaries executed under
.Fl U
do not regain privileges.
If Landlock is unavailable
.Pq kernel older than 5.13 ,
.Fl U
fails closed: the first path is refused and
.Nm
exits with an error before executing the command.
.It Fl u Ar user
Execute the command as
.Ar user .
The default is root.
The target account's PAM account state is not checked; only the
authenticating user's is.
This matches
.Ox
behavior.
.It Fl -
End option parsing.
Use this when the command has its own flags:
.Dq Li "doas -- /usr/bin/pacman -Qi bash" .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std doas
It may fail for one of the following reasons:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The config file
.Pa /etc/doas.conf
could not be parsed.
.It
The user attempted to run a command which is not permitted.
.It
The password was incorrect.
.It
The specified command was not found or is not executable.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr doas.conf 5 ,
.Xr pam.d 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in
.Ox 5.8 .
.Pp
The Linux port
.Pq Nm doas-linux
tracks
.Ox
doas.c 1.100 and doas.1 1.26.
It replaces BSD authentication with PAM and
.Xr login.conf 5
with a compile-time
.Ev PATH .
It adds
.Fl U
and
.Fl P
flags and the
.Ic set getopt
directive, which have no
.Ox
equivalent.
Unlike
.Ox ,
rule matching in
.Xr doas.conf 5
uses the last matching rule rather than the first.
